# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) and edit as needed.
#
# Two independent knobs control where the sync runs and where the frontend
# tries to connect. They are NOT linked — set both consistently.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (Vite) → consumed by src/jazz/provider.tsx at build / dev-server time
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WebSocket URL the browser uses to reach the sync server.
#   - Default (no override): ws://localhost:4200
#   - For a phone / laptop on the same LAN, set to ws://<this-machine-ip>:4200
#   - For a public deployment with TLS, set to wss://sync.example.com
#
# Must start with ws:// or wss://. Vite only exposes env vars prefixed VITE_.
# VITE_SYNC_URL=ws://192.168.1.42:4200

# Comma-separated host allowlist for Vite's dev server. Vite defaults to
# localhost-only and blocks requests with any other Host header to defend
# against DNS-rebinding attacks. Set this when the dev server is reached
# through a hostname Vite doesn't know about (Tailscale Serve, ngrok,
# nip.io, etc.). `scripts/dev-all.sh` sets it automatically when
# Tailscale Serve is configured for port 5173.
#
#   one host:        VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=nox-work.tail06a0b7.ts.net
#   multiple:        VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=host-a.ts.net,host-b.ts.net
#   subdomain glob:  VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=.tail06a0b7.ts.net   (leading dot
#                    matches any *.tail06a0b7.ts.net)
#   allow any:       VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=*                    (dev convenience
#                    only; never set in production)
# VITE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=.tail06a0b7.ts.net

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sync server (scripts/sync-server.sh) → consumed at npm run sync
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interface the sync server binds to.
#   - Default (no override): 127.0.0.1 — localhost only, unreachable from other
#     devices. Safe.
#   - 0.0.0.0 — listen on every interface; other devices on the LAN can connect
#     via this machine's IP. Don't do this on an untrusted network.
# SYNC_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Port the sync server listens on. Default 4200. Change only if it clashes.
# SYNC_PORT=4200

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite dev server (not driven by .env — pass via CLI flag)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite binds to localhost by default. To expose the dev server on the LAN:
#     npm run dev -- --host
# That prints both the local and the LAN URL. Combine with SYNC_HOST=0.0.0.0
# + VITE_SYNC_URL=ws://<this-machine-ip>:4200 for cross-device testing.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth server (scripts/auth-server.sh, deploy/Dockerfile.auth) — Better Auth
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated allowlist of origins Better Auth treats as trusted for
# CSRF / OAuth callback purposes. The default trust covers the origin of
# BETTER_AUTH_URL. Add other origins (e.g. a Tailscale Serve HTTPS URL)
# when the SPA is reached from outside that default. Read natively by
# Better Auth (no code change). `scripts/dev-all.sh` sets this automatically
# when Tailscale Serve is detected.
#
# BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://nox-work.tail06a0b7.ts.net,https://staging.example.com
